# events.zd — what a handler receives (spec §4.4 `handler`, §16.3.7).
#
# Before this, `on click` emitted a zero-argument arrow: a handler could
# say *that* something happened and never *what*. `on click with press`
# binds the event, and the binder is an ordinary name over an ordinary
# body — `with` already introduces binders in `function f with a`,
# `component C with label` and `Archived with reason`, so this production
# costs no reserved word.
#
# Four things it exists to demonstrate:
#
#   1. A payload is typed, and typed per event. `press.x` is a `Decimal`
#      on a click and does not exist on a keystroke; `stroke.key` is a
#      `Text` on a keystroke and does not exist on a click. The set of
#      events is closed, so both of those are compile errors rather than
#      `undefined` at three in the morning.
#   2. A field's contents are reachable at the moment of an event, which
#      is what "commit on blur" needs and what nothing but the two-way
#      binding could reach before.
#   3. Modifier keys are part of the payload, so a shortcut is a program
#      rather than a wish.
#   4. `Input name` is still written the way it always was. It is now
#      sugar for a handler with a payload rather than a special case in
#      the emitter — the same table decides what `value` means for both.
#
# What is deliberately absent: `preventDefault` and `stopPropagation`.
# See the crate report; the short version is that no built-in element has
# a default action to prevent, `Button` being emitted `type="button"`
# precisely so that it has none.

state typed is client Text starting ""
state committed is client Text starting "nothing yet"
state lastKey is client Text starting "none"
state shortcuts is client Whole starting 0
state x is client Decimal starting 0
state y is client Decimal starting 0

view
    Column
        Heading "Event payloads"

        # `Input` wires `on input` itself, so a second handler for the same
        # event is refused (§16.3.6). `keydown` and `blur` are free.
        Input typed
            on keydown with stroke
                set lastKey to stroke.key
                if stroke.control
                    add 1 to shortcuts
            on blur with leaving
                set committed to leaving.value

        Row
            Text "last key: "
            Text lastKey
        Row
            Text "control chords: "
            Text shortcuts
        Row
            Text "committed: "
            Text committed

        Button "where did I land?"
            on click with press
                set x to press.x
                set y to press.y

        Row
            Text "x: "
            Text x
            Text " y: "
            Text y
